      "hint": "Fix coordinates once, pinned point at the origin; never restart the setup. For fixed-area pieces, union = sum minus overlap, so maximize the union by minimizing overlap. Beware the trap of assuming the bigger shape swallows the smaller one: a polygon vertex is only a wedge of its interior angle, so beyond that apex the shape covers nothing. Test one concrete point on the far side before concluding containment. When the apex sits at a center of n-fold rotational symmetry, that 2pi/n wedge cuts off exactly 1/n of the region at every rotation angle, so there is nothing to optimize. Then commit to one exact fraction and stop.",
