      "hint": "Trap: asserting symmetry. \"Each item is equally likely in any position\", or \"n! orderings so 1/n!\", is a guess. A process random over MOVES is rarely uniform over OUTCOMES.\n\nInstead: (1) Pin mechanics first — what move is legal, which item it touches (top of stack only?), and whether the target position means the FIRST or LAST arrival. Derive that from the stacking rule; never guess. (2) Turn the event into an exact constraint on the move sequence, e.g. \"moves strictly alternate\" or \"exactly k source-moves precede the first sink-move\". (3) Count only genuinely free 50/50 choices; forced moves (source or sink empty) contribute factor 1, giving 1/2^(free choices), not 1/n or 1/n!. (4) Check n=2 by full enumeration. Re-derive each part from scratch — same setup, different constraint.",
